+## Setup
+
+Use Node.js 24, as required by package.json. There are no package dependencies to
+install. Open a terminal at the repository root; npm can run the declared scripts,
+or Node can run the entry point directly.
+
+## Usage
+
+```sh
+node src/cli.mjs test/parcels.ndjson
+# Equivalent project script:
+npm run preview -- test/parcels.ndjson
+```
+
+The supplied synthetic input has one ready parcel (`demo-101`) and one already
+dispatched parcel (`demo-102`). The observed preview is:
+
+```json
+{"parcelId":"demo-101","action":"dispatch"}
+```
+
+For another input file, supply one JSON object on each nonblank line. A ready
+record must have a nonempty string `id`; non-ready statuses are ignored. Missing
+a filename prints usage and exits with code 2. File-reading errors, malformed
+JSON, and invalid ready IDs fail the command. Output is not persisted: rerunning
+a file emits its ready previews again, so callers must not treat this tool as
+an idempotent carrier submission service.
+
+## Development
+
+Run `npm test`. Both dispatch tests passed on this Linux checkout: ready-only
+selection and rejection of a ready parcel without an ID. Source ownership and
+the input-to-output path are described in [src/README.md](src/README.md).
+
+Use synthetic records in examples, keep customer addresses private, and obtain
+warehouse-platform owner review for production changes. Carrier integration
+changes remain subject to release-manager scheduling.
