+# Parcel preview data flow
+
+The entry point is `cli.mjs`. Its responsibility is process I/O: require an input
+filename, read the file, ignore blank lines, parse each JSON object, and print
+one serialized result per line. It delegates selection to `pendingDispatches`
+from `dispatch.mjs`.
+
+`dispatch.mjs` contains the parcel rule: only `ready` records proceed, their IDs
+must be nonempty strings, and results contain `parcelId` plus action `dispatch`.
+The transformation preserves the order of selected inputs and performs no I/O.
+
+Keep filesystem/argument concerns at the CLI boundary and parcel-selection logic
+in the transformation. `test/dispatch.test.mjs` covers that logic;
+`test/parcels.ndjson` demonstrates the CLI. Neither module contacts carriers or
+updates the source file, and there is no durable queue state in these modules.
